// endpoint_fold_held_prompt.proto — FoldHeldPrompt: FOLDING a held prompt into
// the held prompt directly ahead of it. DAEMON-HOLD TRAY section.
//
// The tray card's "fold above" button sends it. The folded prompt's content
// (text, images and every other block it carries, in order) is appended to the
// entry ahead of it, separated from that entry's own words by a blank line, and
// the folded prompt leaves the queue. The entry ahead keeps its place in the
// queue and its identity (its turn, its origin, its target, its delivery), so
// the two are delivered together, as that one entry, when its turn comes.
//
// ONE TRANSACTION. The merged content and the folded prompt's retirement are
// written in one durable transaction, so no reader ever sees both prompts
// standing with the merged text, or the folded prompt gone with nothing merged.
//
// THE MERGED ENTRY IS JUDGED AFRESH, exactly as an edit's commit is judged: its
// standing verdict and its acceptance are discarded, a verdict still being
// reached about its old words is discarded when it lands, and it is
// reclassified through the ordinary classifier path. A verdict reached on the
// old words never applies to the new ones.
//
// BOTH ENTRIES ARE NAMED BY TYPED ECHO TOKENS: `turn` is the folded prompt's
// own TurnId from its tray entry, and `above` is the TurnId the same entry's
// HeldPromptFoldAbove carried. The daemon folds into `above` and nothing else:
// when `above` is no longer the entry directly ahead, the request is refused
// and nothing is folded, so a prompt is never folded into an entry the user
// did not see above it.
//
// NOT THIS: joining the RUNNING turn. A prompt cannot be folded into a turn
// that has started; that is the classifier's after_tool_call verdict, which
// sends the prompt into the running turn at its next tool boundary.

